WEBVTT

00:02:28.204 --> 00:02:32.413
The effects of stress can even
seep into the DNA of your brain.

00:02:32.829 --> 00:02:34.121
An experiment has shown

00:02:34.163 --> 00:02:37.371
that the amount of attention
a mother rat gives to her newborn

00:02:37.413 --> 00:02:42.454
plays an important role in the way
this baby will react to stress later on.

00:02:42.788 --> 00:02:46.704
The offsprings of caring mothers
were found to be less sensitive to stress

00:02:46.746 --> 00:02:50.121
because their brains developed
more cortisol receptors

00:02:50.163 --> 00:02:54.121
which fix cortisol and reduce 
the stress response.

00:02:54.746 --> 00:02:58.163
The offsprings of neglectful mothers
had the opposite reaction,

00:02:58.204 --> 00:03:01.579
so they are more sensitive
to stress during their lifetime.